    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'equal' (adjective) has a broad meaning, encompassing 'identical,' 'same in quantity/value,' and 'fair/impartial.' While '同一' (douitsu) can mean 'equal' in the sense of 'identical' or 'the same' (as reflected in its JMdict glosses), it is semantically narrower than the general English adjective. For a general learner, '同一' would not be the most natural or common translation for all contexts of 'equal.' For instance, '等しい' (hitoshii) is more commonly used for 'equal in quantity or value,' and '平等' (byoudou) for 'equal/fair treatment.' Therefore, '同一' is a narrower fit for the general concept of 'equal.'",
